    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0495" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1944v02/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.796/879: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Winant</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-05-31T22:00:00+02:00">May 31, 1944—10
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:33 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4371. Hildred says that his proposed trip to the United States to discuss
                    technical matters mentioned in Embassy’s telegram No. 3573, May 1, 10 p.m.,
                    although approved by the Air Minister, has been held up by Beaverbrook who does
                    not wish to let the technical phases of aviation discussions pass completely out
                    of his hands. Hildred has <pb facs="0496" n="486" xml:id="pg486"/> written a
                    long letter to Warner<anchor n="24" xml:id="d388-f1"/> outlining the subjects he
                    wishes to discuss or have discussed in Washington and believes that if Warner
                    replies favorably, expressing the hope that Hildred can come to Washington,
                    approval will be secured for his trip. We feel that the comments contained in
                    our 3573 of May 1 still hold good. This message is most secret.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Winant</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
